## Screens & components annotated

**App: WebTestBench_0097 — "CompetencyHub" (job competency modeling, Vite + React + shadcn)**

- **Landing screen** (`Index.tsx`, `JobSearch.tsx`): header nav (`nav.models`, `nav.analytics`), stats collection (`home.stats` + 3 items), search input (`jobs.search.query` → controls `jobs.grid`), department select (`jobs.filter.department` with `data-semtag-options` built from the same `departments` array that renders the menu, plus `option` items keyed by slugged value), job card grid (`jobs.grid` collection, items keyed by model id, per-item `.department` / `.competency-count` observables), empty-state message (`jobs.search.empty`).
- **Model detail screen** (`ModelDetailView.tsx`): back navigation, title/department/count observables, `export`/`share`/`save` actions.
- **Metrics** (`MetricsPanel.tsx`): `model.metrics` region; `metrics.coverage`, `metrics.avg-level`, `metrics.critical-path.count`, `metrics.gaps.count` observables; conditional `metrics.gap-alert` / `metrics.healthy-alert`.
- **Competency graph** (`CompetencyGraph.tsx` + `CompetencyNode.tsx`): `model.graph` collection wrapping the ReactFlow canvas; per-competency items keyed by domain id (`model.graph.item.prog-lang` …) with `.enabled` toggle, `.set-level-1…5` actions (the unlabeled level bars — now reachable by id alone), `.level-value` / `.weight-value` observables, and `.weight` slider sharing state key `competency.weight` with its display.
- **Simulation panel** (`SimulationPanel.tsx`): region, scenario tabs as navigation (`simulation.scenario.<type>`), active-scenario observable, `simulation.adjustments` collection with items keyed by category and `.level` / `.weight` sliders paired to `.level-value` / `.weight-value` observables via shared state keys, `simulation.run` / `simulation.reset` actions.
- **Template library** (`TemplateLibrary.tsx`): `templates.list` collection keyed by template id, `.apply` action and conditional `.current` badge per item, `templates.save-current` action.
- **NotFound page**: message observable + home link.

